            <ArticleTitle>Enhanced Nonenzymatic RNA Copying with 2-Aminoimidazole Activated Nucleotides.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1810-1813</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1021/jacs.6b13148</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Achieving efficient nonenzymatic replication of RNA is an important step toward the synthesis of self-replicating protocells that may mimic early forms of life. Despite recent progress, the nonenzymatic copying of templates containing mixed sequences remains slow and inefficient. Here we demonstrate that activating nucleotides with 2-aminoimidazole results in superior reaction kinetics and improved yields of primer extension reaction products. This new leaving group significantly accelerates monomer addition as well as trimer-assisted RNA primer extension, allowing efficient copying of a variety of short RNA templates with mixed sequences.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
